#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133829 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133644 :question/id #uuid "f07dd3d3-606f-520f-a95e-04303aa32f24" :question/math-academy-id "e-6307" :question/problem "Find an integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf r(t)= \\left \\langle \\cos t, \\sin t \\right\\rangle$ for $t \\in \\left(0, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f5/f53d78debfec5f8c50e0f3a5947d2a36126e18c073d7b0cc4c59d506753059b3.png)\n\nThe path of integration is shown above. We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $f(x,y) =  xy^3$. Along the path, we have $x=\\cos t$ and $y=\\sin t,$ and so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =f(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{3} \\\\  & ={sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s = \\int^{\\pi/2}_{0} \\sin^3 t \\cos t \\, \\textrm{d}t .\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f7479a-a84c-59fa-a7ea-9377c7e65b19" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048418}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539206 :question-generator/id #uuid "dd3dfc48-9a48-5a88-b422-3e3f29557457" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186133829.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e006fbf-73db-5714-80d3-da70e1961752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324338} {:answer/id #uuid "4454bda2-b710-5b8e-962a-af8f72db9bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324524} {:answer/id #uuid "969d3d60-bae9-5b94-bb58-6e2e78279810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325255} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88ce8a-6d69-5cce-ae62-6e652a14c027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325896} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fc0716-e381-59ad-99c7-f5348e2706dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e006fbf-73db-5714-80d3-da70e1961752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324338} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa3112f0-f6c4-537c-b0c9-7b639ee76cae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13f50e74-e351-581a-98f5-c8e27aa5380d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40253" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized \n by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+t,$ and $y={t}^{2}-t.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)j \\\\  & =(2t+1)\\,i+(2t-1)\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t+1)^{2}+(2t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4t+1+4{t}^{2}-4t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{2}[({t}^{2}+t)-({t}^{2}-t)] \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f149a5c8-374a-5613-9e94-f7a85f4e3578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} + t - 2)dt$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133117} {:answer/id #uuid "07f01a2c-6102-5f57-9a81-827ca9995533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(4t^{3} - 3)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133118} {:answer/id #uuid "0e53f525-69b5-5819-9c6b-7b1f40a1280e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(t^{3} - t^{2} + 4t)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133119} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8c7275-20d2-58af-b910-a3018cd7a77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} - t^{2} + 4t - 4)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133120} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb682b0-7b0d-59e5-8435-a35378e856c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} + t^{2} - 4)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133121}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee84ab5-a5cf-5da3-83b7-b25c4dfcdc31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133116}] :question/id #uuid "2f8d1c23-74d2-5539-9285-abeec9fd6ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76368" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)(x^{3} - y)ds$, where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = 2ti + (2 - t)j$ for $-1 \\le t \\le 2$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263de2e3-27ae-52e2-8582-4dfb39ba6ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282023} {:answer/id #uuid "75614e75-3308-50a7-a253-f1f9b76e3296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282694} {:answer/id #uuid "76433ca0-b7f8-577e-a495-c0ae272242e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282701} {:answer/id #uuid "89172764-a6f4-5672-8136-d35db577b74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t(2t+1)\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282872} {:answer/id #uuid "8caffd9e-930e-5e4b-b97e-bcbc15c29c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76433ca0-b7f8-577e-a495-c0ae272242e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282701} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee764035-aa19-5d16-9448-a4b9dd4171f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bb4ae8a-0b75-5e62-bc9b-0900b739960b" :question/math-academy-id "q-167608" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $0\\le t\\le 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{4y+1}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "372a5048-17c2-5076-9635-4ff4ad531da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t-1)\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342693} {:answer/id #uuid "60710012-7ccb-54d9-aac8-7c21a4db39de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343056} {:answer/id #uuid "7143c54a-f0e9-502c-b646-975daaf14a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343209} {:answer/id #uuid "77d755de-6003-5532-a85f-2d9e8cb137d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}-2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343274} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8c1d1a-5321-50f7-aff8-7b81e9c745ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60710012-7ccb-54d9-aac8-7c21a4db39de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343056} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d47b24e-5186-5a2c-bc62-0a4991b4b99e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e477990a-d15e-595b-a078-39c7382f9c05" :question/math-academy-id "q-76377" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2},$ $y=t-1,$ and $z=t+1.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2({t}^{2})-(t-1)^{2}-(t+1)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-({t}^{2}-2t+1)-({t}^{2}+2t+1) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}+2t-1-{t}^{2}-2t-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2(2{t}^{2}+1)}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f72ef384-5e6e-52c5-839e-3beee185405e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393620} {:answer/id #uuid "42147aee-d1b6-54a9-a34c-6883f2cfc5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393621} {:answer/id #uuid "38308454-7a76-5601-988c-cc81a2d49d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}-t)\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393622} {:answer/id #uuid "9d940168-caf2-55dc-abc9-6478a8eb7fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393623} {:answer/id #uuid "89f9a881-2016-5d9d-b0c2-417ca0dbf7d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42147aee-d1b6-54a9-a34c-6883f2cfc5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393621} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc0d4305-f486-5b23-8a23-7975fef766e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dd51c2a-c921-500f-b456-d9efa51cbc02" :question/math-academy-id "q-76356" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+1,$ $y={t}^{2}-1,$ and $z={t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}|t| \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t>0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =({t}^{2}+1)+({t}^{2}-1)-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}t\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa31ddbb-d2dc-5e24-b119-3e57906a0e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393627} {:answer/id #uuid "6e191add-76d4-52b0-a4d0-b55782dad06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393628} {:answer/id #uuid "e78b94bc-a9b3-5508-8e70-1864ef024d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393629} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7e2485-49a8-54d2-9942-acfa1e262b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393630} {:answer/id #uuid "1e167558-c450-5d8c-885f-dd7f2edd9925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e191add-76d4-52b0-a4d0-b55782dad06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393628} :answer-field/id #uuid "80947165-9047-5b9a-b812-2946d21a42e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfad2296-6fbf-598f-a4ed-63e51e9c1622" :question/math-academy-id "q-76379" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k$ for $\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ and $z=t.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, if $f(x,y,z)=z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}) \\\\  & =t({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1da427-cfa7-5281-8204-d21535a2e929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13} \\left(6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539136} {:answer/id #uuid "35771a76-e706-5927-92ab-462e6d1f85c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539138} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2e2937-ae52-5040-b66a-a5c64838d0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}- 3 \\left(4 t^{2} + 13\\right) \\left(- 2 t^{3} + 8 t^{2} + 6 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539142} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9e8407-ee17-513a-9905-7a045102dae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13} \\left(t^{2} \\left(2 t + 1\\right) + \\left(3 t + 1\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539147} {:answer/id #uuid "8353a5ce-5ec8-58d9-82a4-deeedafa3521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\frac{3 \\left(2 t^{3} - 8 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1da427-cfa7-5281-8204-d21535a2e929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13} \\left(6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539136} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d63b3a0-c096-5219-817e-9b3bad04d2cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "021666da-2b39-563b-b7fb-5efa8b86fda8" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C 3 x y - 3 z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2}, 2 t + 1, 3 t + 1\\rangle$ for $\\frac{1}{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{3}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle t^{2}, 2 t + 1, 3 t + 1\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=2 t + 1$, $z=3 t + 1$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 1)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t + 1)k \\\\ &= (2 t)\\,i+(2)\\,j+(3)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(2)^2+(3)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=3 x y - 3 z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=3\\left((t^{2})(2 t + 1)-(3 t + 1)^2\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\left(2t^3+(1)t^2-\\left(9t^2+(6)t+1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= 6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}(6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 13} \\left(6 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} - 18 t - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bbf45e-712a-50fc-9c7f-3db24fc3f7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\frac{2 \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539127} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8011db-7762-523b-8d12-4da85216dfd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}- 2 t^{3} + 14 t^{2} + 8 t + 2\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539149} {:answer/id #uuid "a46660c1-17ae-5ef0-8a37-70323fa5fabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- t^{3} - t^{2} - 4 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539175} {:answer/id #uuid "ad8ff517-6e7d-547d-aa23-f428cf620502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\left(4 t^{2} + 5\\right) \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539179} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc8dcdb-9950-52f1-b6f2-4fb28f2f94be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc8dcdb-9950-52f1-b6f2-4fb28f2f94be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539193} :answer-field/id #uuid "69673806-2d1a-558a-87aa-962b7675aa65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19471cdf-9ea5-5c33-ad36-e0767c3ac883" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C - 2 x y + 2 z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2}, t - 3, 2 t + 1\\rangle$ for $1\\le t\\le \\frac{3}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle t^{2}, t - 3, 2 t + 1\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t - 3$, $z=2 t + 1$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 3)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 1)k \\\\ &= (2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(2)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2+(2)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + 2 z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=-2\\left((t^{2})(t - 3)-(2 t + 1)^2\\right) \\\\ &= -2\\left(1t^3+(-3)t^2-\\left(4t^2+(4)t+1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= - 2 t^{3} + 14 t^{2} + 8 t + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}(- 2 t^{3} + 14 t^{2} + 8 t + 2)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c637e7-9d1d-5a19-bf0e-0dfdcc062824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\frac{4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1}{\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539139} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa6780b-c1c7-5d0f-bc04-322cd3efb4a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539152} {:answer/id #uuid "805163b1-91d9-5657-84ba-f0adcd279e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}- \\left(16 t^{2} + 13\\right) \\left(- 4 t^{3} + 5 t^{2} + 6 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539167} {:answer/id #uuid "c792bb24-aaaf-56f9-a31e-683b56a1218d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13} \\left(4 t^{2} \\left(t + 1\\right) + \\left(3 t + 1\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539186} {:answer/id #uuid "d82355ef-7111-535b-bc6f-528e24822529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13} \\left(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d82355ef-7111-535b-bc6f-528e24822529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13} \\left(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539191} :answer-field/id #uuid "507606cb-45d1-5506-805d-8a68afcce084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b6b1bd1-88e4-5d2e-9dfb-33372f16d858" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C x y - z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 2, 3 t + 1\\rangle$ for $0\\le t\\le 2$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 2, 3 t + 1\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t^{2}$, $y=2 t + 2$, $z=3 t + 1$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 2)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t + 1)k \\\\ &= (4 t)\\,i+(2)\\,j+(3)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(4 t)^2+(2)^2+(3)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x y - z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2 t^{2})(2 t + 2)-(3 t + 1)^2 \\\\ &= 4t^3+(4)t^2-\\left(9t^2+(6)t+1\\right) \\\\ &= 4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{2}(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1)(\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13} \\left(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a182349-c6b0-5892-a095-c61253000a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t}{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539151} {:answer/id #uuid "808a5bee-fd16-5441-99c5-68b38ff67c63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539168} {:answer/id #uuid "9950a772-8737-542f-989a-2f5006693b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t}{\\left(4 t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539173} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a1d7be-903b-525d-a61b-b6fd648c3cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539177} {:answer/id #uuid "e8983d55-5bea-5b37-b969-63bf075c738a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8983d55-5bea-5b37-b969-63bf075c738a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539199} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d2f535-cd02-5984-8b38-b25fd712257c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "629bb41a-481a-5fce-89d8-1176b4e371da" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $0\\le t\\le 5?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\left(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t  \\\\    & =2\\left({\\int }_{0}^{5}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right) \\\\    & =2\\left({\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278b3e92-0930-54df-8b78-9d1eb2eb134a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{2} t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539133} {:answer/id #uuid "27d15098-9f4d-5025-b663-55253273ac10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539134} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e304d5-2e98-55e6-88b1-e67c5a9ca1c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539194} {:answer/id #uuid "e45f8e18-3e75-5cb3-8aee-472302b82414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539195} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1b2043-64b1-5186-9ca4-d5be02457609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}2 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e45f8e18-3e75-5cb3-8aee-472302b82414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539195} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1b51734-7cf3-59d4-b15c-c37a8d472ced" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77c0932d-edde-5a3d-a95b-c9e88ef0198f" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k$ for $\\,\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ and $z=t.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, if $f(x,y,z)=z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}) \\\\  & =t({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{12}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbf7d63-fae5-55c0-b85a-adf23a9e249f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539130} {:answer/id #uuid "45af7fa4-3c7f-5937-a136-75ca8b278b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}2 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539144} {:answer/id #uuid "b21d5ca9-b166-5274-a50b-458ef7c02100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t}{\\left(4 t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539181} {:answer/id #uuid "c9985de4-28ed-5456-ad68-a38e965bae9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539187} {:answer/id #uuid "e55bbb40-be6b-5a87-aca7-130550b420f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t}{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9985de4-28ed-5456-ad68-a38e965bae9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539187} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ce0eb2-a951-5877-b687-deea0d30c7a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86c6a686-849e-56ac-8cd5-66fc10eebbef" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $2\\le t\\le \\frac{11}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\left(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t  \\\\    & =2\\left({\\int }_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right) \\\\    & =2\\left({\\int }_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ddac435-f4c5-5790-a848-0d7fd8aecc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}10 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539131} {:answer/id #uuid "49e747ab-2e87-5b28-b3b1-52bfbfa14251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}5 \\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539145} {:answer/id #uuid "4a119ce1-666c-589c-913e-71a12513c765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\frac{5 \\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539146} {:answer/id #uuid "7f1d6599-ceb5-5eed-83dc-ed06fd4e1d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}5 \\sqrt{2} t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539165} {:answer/id #uuid "804f7a7d-ca0c-5b72-99dd-1e2bd2065c4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}5 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49e747ab-2e87-5b28-b3b1-52bfbfa14251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}5 \\sqrt{2} t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539145} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4985361-8dc5-544a-a26a-fb6bff95a3f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88d1c090-6bb7-523f-a9f3-d7ec7807cd7a" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}5\\left(z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\right)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k$ for $\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi}{6}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ and $z=t.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, if $f(x,y,z)=5\\left(z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\right)$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5\\left(t((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2})\\right) \\\\    & =5\\left(t({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\right) \\\\    & =5\\left(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}5\\left(z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\right)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t  \\\\    & =5\\left({\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right) \\\\    & =5\\left(\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ec66b2-9271-5a86-bba6-39b76534dbf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{5 t}{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539124} {:answer/id #uuid "39eb83de-83c7-5476-b2e1-42b4fe358621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}5 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539140} {:answer/id #uuid "3a918622-26b5-5fae-b7b9-05af71744ab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{5 t}{\\left(4 t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539141} {:answer/id #uuid "60aab06d-1253-59b6-b9bd-40fdc6f9eb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{5 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539156} {:answer/id #uuid "7b390292-66dd-5f10-a384-8ca7ed8cf17b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{5 t^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60aab06d-1253-59b6-b9bd-40fdc6f9eb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{5 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539156} :answer-field/id #uuid "af41d808-87d0-52a5-979b-295e732e80de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a17cfaab-14e7-5c09-ade5-3176e170f53b" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}5\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $\\frac{1}{2}\\le t\\le \\frac{7}{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=5\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5\\left(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}5\\left(\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\right)\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t  \\\\    & =5\\left({\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t\\right) \\\\    & =5\\left({\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{\\frac{7}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6007b4c8-5fd7-5182-b9b1-b8ab65716cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539155} {:answer/id #uuid "c10d389c-0aa7-5b23-82b4-246c7ac9ce69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}- 2 \\left(36 t^{2} + 5\\right) \\left(3 t^{3} + 5 t^{2} - 8 t - 4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539184} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c7ac66-9df2-5528-8428-8ab1dc9902f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\frac{2 \\left(- 3 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} + 8 t + 4\\right)}{\\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539190} {:answer/id #uuid "df5c3f33-dfe4-50f6-8249-42490daafec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}- 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539192} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a7e9b2-2d21-55ba-a040-b5b1c6d8da08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}2 \\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- 3 t^{2} \\left(t + 3\\right) - 4 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6007b4c8-5fd7-5182-b9b1-b8ab65716cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539155} :answer-field/id #uuid "66661945-6b6a-5b27-bb7a-9979aec89f63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a908ad08-fd2d-5338-a3b2-fa3636e47ff4" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C - 2 x y + 2 z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle 3 t^{2}, t + 3, 2 t + 2\\rangle$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{5}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle 3 t^{2}, t + 3, 2 t + 2\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=3 t^{2}$, $y=t + 3$, $z=2 t + 2$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t + 3)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 2)k \\\\ &= (6 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(2)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(6 t)^2+(1)^2+(2)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + 2 z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=-2\\left((3 t^{2})(t + 3)-(2 t + 2)^2\\right) \\\\ &= -2\\left(3t^3+(9)t^2-\\left(4t^2+(8)t+4\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= - 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}(- 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8)(\\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}\\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- 6 t^{3} - 10 t^{2} + 16 t + 8\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d55e55-4da0-5e7e-b523-3a71c34060d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}t\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539135} {:answer/id #uuid "7b5b324f-dc6f-5f53-96c6-b0679ba8cf94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539163} {:answer/id #uuid "8698b24c-571c-586d-9aa9-791ca92cca74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\left(4 t^{2} + 1\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539170} {:answer/id #uuid "b26b07de-bd8f-5b41-9dc8-2063df8ca6ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539182} {:answer/id #uuid "d04b5623-2bff-542f-8d52-93366f70ddc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d04b5623-2bff-542f-8d52-93366f70ddc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539188} :answer-field/id #uuid "06daf866-2151-53ab-a697-9d6282e0ae9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f04c0a98-4a6c-5873-883f-948e18d8b72b" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $1\\le t\\le \\frac{4}{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{4y+1}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0228b294-5832-5825-ad8a-3bc0a9bdbe23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)}{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539123} {:answer/id #uuid "0f75487c-a5f1-5e36-86b8-989567defbd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}80 t^{3} + 10 t - 20\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539126} {:answer/id #uuid "7dea96ab-5a7e-592e-944f-a693c36c797b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}16 t^{3} + 2 t - 4\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539164} {:answer/id #uuid "c6680a8a-cce7-55d0-b883-50e0e3ba2e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} - t + 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539185} {:answer/id #uuid "f38f729c-48d5-5112-b120-4a7a2e085fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f38f729c-48d5-5112-b120-4a7a2e085fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539201} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97f8f35-3ac8-510f-857f-73a5203bed44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f515b153-b2d5-5f07-b698-2b223e35049e" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_C2\\left((x^{3} - y)\\right)ds$, where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = 2ti + (2 - t)j$ for $- \\frac{3}{2}\\le t\\le 2$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle 2 t, 2 - t\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t$, $y=2 - t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 - t)j \\\\ &= (2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(-1)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2 x^{3} - 2 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=2\\left((2 t)^3-(2 - t)\\right) \\\\ &= 2\\left(8t^3-2+t\\right) \\\\ &= 16 t^{3} + 2 t - 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}(16 t^{3} + 2 t - 4)(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30338bca-6ca0-51af-8f2f-96eb86969268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}12 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 18 t - 27\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539137} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9fac12-ab2b-5bd8-ac50-2e5e3c1a9b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5} \\left(4 t^{3} + t^{2} - 6 t - 9\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539148} {:answer/id #uuid "5d90c9ff-4b45-5a51-ad47-6931f43284f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5} \\left(2 t^{2} \\left(2 t + 1\\right) + \\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539154} {:answer/id #uuid "741d6ee7-19d1-5aef-a755-d8ed6ebfa877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\frac{3 \\left(4 t^{3} + t^{2} - 6 t - 9\\right)}{\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539160} {:answer/id #uuid "a543efd7-e7a5-5a36-9b77-3946d717a988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\left(16 t^{2} + 5\\right) \\left(4 t^{3} + t^{2} - 6 t - 9\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9fac12-ab2b-5bd8-ac50-2e5e3c1a9b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5} \\left(4 t^{3} + t^{2} - 6 t - 9\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539148} :answer-field/id #uuid "4103d898-eeb8-573e-bb32-54b6347b1152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fcd80b68-90ad-5381-82bb-4a395bb5f45b" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C 3 x y - 3 z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 1, t + 3\\rangle$ for $1\\le t\\le \\frac{3}{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 1, t + 3\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t^{2}$, $y=2 t + 1$, $z=t + 3$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 1)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t + 3)k \\\\ &= (4 t)\\,i+(2)\\,j+(1)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(4 t)^2+(2)^2+(1)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=3 x y - 3 z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=3\\left((2 t^{2})(2 t + 1)-(t + 3)^2\\right) \\\\ &= 3\\left(4t^3+(2)t^2-\\left(1t^2+(6)t+9\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= 12 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 18 t - 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}(12 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 18 t - 27)(\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}3 \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 5} \\left(4 t^{3} + t^{2} - 6 t - 9\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Line Integral of a Scalar Function as a Definite Integral"}]}
